-- חוזר לבעלויות תשע"ג/1: היערכות לפתיחת שנת הלימודים תשע"ג בתאריך 27/8/2012 (11.9.2012)
-- Salary in the transition month after school year 2012/13 opened early on
-- 27.8.2012: the five days of August paid as the new year's, for teachers
-- who continue with the employer, new teachers and teachers who left; the
-- days offset for the extra vacation of 2011/12 by the date of leaving; and
-- the September adjustment by the difference in the day rate.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT common

§ `תשע"ג/1 היערכות לפתיחת שנת הלימודים תשע"ג בתאריך 27/8/2012`

-- akn:preamble The letterhead, title, date (11.9.2012), addressee and subject line; no rule of its own. Its background paragraphs are encoded below.

-- Time on the timeline of the regulative rules is counted in school months
-- of 2011/12 (September 2011 = 1, August 2012 = 12, September 2012 = 13,
-- October 2012 = 14).

@desc A teaching employee at the turn of school years 2011/12 and 2012/13, as far as this circular asks about it.
DECLARE `transition teacher` HAS
    `situation`                          IS A `transition situation`
    `August salary on the 2011/12 basis` IS A NUMBER @desc the monthly salary for 8/2012 computed on the salary paid in 2011/12, shekels
    `day rate in August 2012`            IS A NUMBER @desc the rate of one working day in August 2012, shekels
    `day rate in September 2012`         IS A NUMBER @desc the rate of one working day in September 2012, by the employment data of that month, shekels
    `position, grade, seniority or allowances changed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc between the two school years
    `on maternity leave from 27.8.2012`  IS A BOOLEAN @desc on maternity leave in the five August days of the new year
    `hired from the August 2012 salary`  IS A BOOLEAN @desc a new teacher taken on from the August 2012 salary
    `date of leaving`                    IS A DATE @desc for a teacher who left or retired: the date of leaving or retirement

@desc The three cases section א divides teachers into.
DECLARE `transition situation` IS ONE OF
    `continuing with the same employer`
    `new with the employer in 2012/13`
    `left or retired from 2011/12`

DECLARE `transition action` IS ONE OF
    `pay the August salary` HAS `August paid` IS A NUMBER
    `pay or offset the September difference` HAS `difference settled` IS A NUMBER
    `pay the five extra days` HAS `extra days paid` IS A NUMBER
    `offset the extra vacation days` HAS `vacation offset` IS A NUMBER

§§ `רקע`

-- ¶10: by the Minister's decision, 2012/13 opens on 27.8.2012: the salary
-- for 2011/12 ends on 26.8.2012 and the salary for 2012/13 begins on
-- 27.8.2012.
@desc The school year a working day's salary belongs to.
DECLARE `salary year` IS ONE OF
    `2011/12`
    `2012/13`

`the day 2012/13 opens` MEANS Date 27 8 2012

@ref akn:preamble/p10
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A `salary year`
DECIDE `the salary year of the day` d IS
    IF d AT LEAST `the day 2012/13 opens`
    THEN `2012/13`
    ELSE `2011/12`

#ASSERT `the salary year of the day` (Date 26 8 2012) EQUALS `2011/12`
#ASSERT `the salary year of the day` (Date 27 8 2012) EQUALS `2012/13`

-- ¶11-¶13: teachers employed in 2011/12 received 5 extra vacation days on
-- various dates; it was agreed they are returned by opening 2012/13 early.
-- ¶14-¶15: being a transition year, the instructions for August's salary
-- follow; ¶15 is the heading of section א.
@ref akn:preamble/p11 akn:preamble/p12 akn:preamble/p13
`extra vacation days in 2011/12` MEANS 5

-- The five working days of August 2012 that belong to 2012/13 (27-31.8.2012).
`the August days of the new year` MEANS 5

-- akn:preamble/p14 akn:preamble/p15 The lead-in to the instructions and the heading "א. salary for working days in August 2012"; the rules follow.

§§ `1 מורים ממשיכים אצל המעסיק`

-- Section 1: a teacher employed in 2011/12 (all or part of it) who
-- continues with the same employer in 2012/13 is paid the 8/2012 salary in
-- full, without change, on the 2011/12 basis.
@ref akn:art_1
GIVEN t IS A `transition teacher`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the August salary` t IS
    CONSIDER t's `situation`
    WHEN `continuing with the same employer` THEN t's `August salary on the 2011/12 basis`
    WHEN `left or retired from 2011/12`      THEN t's `August salary on the 2011/12 basis`
    OTHERWISE 0

GIVEN t IS A `transition teacher`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `transition action`
DECIDE `paying August in full` t IS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `pay the August salary` `amount`
          PROVIDED `amount` AT LEAST `the August salary` t
    WITHIN 12
    LEST BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "sections 1 and 3: the August 2012 salary is paid in full, without change"

-- Section 1 ¶2 and section 4: with the 9/2012 salary, differences for the
-- five working days of 8/2012 are paid or offset (an update of seniority,
-- grade, allowances and so on). 4(1): a day rate is computed in both months;
-- 4(2): the August rate is carried to the September salary, and an employee
-- whose position (or grade, seniority, allowances) changed is paid or
-- offset the difference between the two rates for five days. 4(3): the
-- five August days are offset for a teacher on maternity leave in them.
@ref akn:art_1/p2 akn:art_4 akn:art_4__para_1 akn:art_4__para_2 akn:art_4__para_2/p2
GIVEN t IS A `transition teacher`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the rate difference for the five days` t IS
    IF t's `position, grade, seniority or allowances changed`
    THEN (t's `day rate in September 2012` MINUS t's `day rate in August 2012`)
         TIMES `the August days of the new year`
    ELSE 0

@ref akn:art_4__para_3
GIVEN t IS A `transition teacher`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the maternity offset` t IS
    IF t's `on maternity leave from 27.8.2012`
    THEN t's `day rate in August 2012` TIMES `the August days of the new year`
    ELSE 0

GIVEN t IS A `transition teacher`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the September difference` t IS
    IF t's `situation` EQUALS `continuing with the same employer`
    THEN `the rate difference for the five days` t MINUS `the maternity offset` t
    ELSE 0

GIVEN t IS A `transition teacher`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `transition action`
DECIDE `settling the difference with September's salary` t IS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `pay or offset the September difference` `amount`
          PROVIDED `amount` EQUALS `the September difference` t
    WITHIN 13
    LEST BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "sections 1 and 4: the differences for the five August days are settled in the September 2012 salary"

§§ `2 מורים חדשים אצל המעסיק`

-- Section 2: it is preferable to take new teachers of 2012/13 on from the
-- 8/2012 salary. Where that is not possible, they are paid five more days at
-- the 9/2012 day rate, by their employment data in 9/2012, with the 9/2012
-- salary paid at the start of 10/2012.
@ref akn:art_2
GIVEN t IS A `transition teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `owed the five extra days` t IF
        t's `situation` EQUALS `new with the employer in 2012/13`
    AND NOT t's `hired from the August 2012 salary`

GIVEN t IS A `transition teacher`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the five extra days` t IS
    IF `owed the five extra days` t
    THEN t's `day rate in September 2012` TIMES `the August days of the new year`
    ELSE 0

GIVEN t IS A `transition teacher`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `transition action`
DECIDE `paying the five extra days` t IS
    IF `owed the five extra days` t
    THEN PARTY `the employer`
         MUST  `pay the five extra days` `amount`
               PROVIDED `amount` AT LEAST `the five extra days` t
         WITHIN 14
         LEST BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "section 2: a new teacher not taken on from August is paid five more days with the 9/2012 salary, paid at the start of 10/2012"
    ELSE FULFILLED

§§ `3 מורים שעזבו/פרשו בסוף שנה"ל תשע"ב`

-- Section 3: for these teachers the Ministry pays August in full, and
-- offsets the extra vacation days received in 2011/12 at the August rate
-- (shown on the slip as "הפרשי הקדמת שנה"ל"), counted by the 2011/12
-- vacation calendar. The table of days by the date of leaving, as printed.
@ref akn:art_3 akn:art_3/p2 akn:art_3/p3 akn:art_3/p4 akn:art_3/p5 akn:art_3/p6 akn:art_3/p7 akn:art_3/p8
DECLARE `leaving row` HAS
    `left from` IS A DATE
    `left until` IS A DATE
    `days offset` IS A NUMBER

`the table of days offset` MEANS
    LIST `leaving row` (Date 1 9 2011)   (Date 9 10 2011)  0,
         `leaving row` (Date 10 10 2011) (Date 20 12 2011) 3,
         `leaving row` (Date 20 12 2011) (Date 29 3 2012)  4,
         `leaving row` (Date 30 3 2012)  (Date 31 8 2012)  5

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
DECIDE `the days the table offsets for leaving on` d IS
    map (GIVEN r YIELD r's `days offset`)
        (filter (GIVEN r YIELD d AT LEAST r's `left from` AND d AT MOST r's `left until`)
                `the table of days offset`)

-- F-2012-13_tashag_01-a: 20.12.2011 closes the second row and opens the
-- third: 3 days and 4.
`leaving on 20.12.2011 is given 3 days and 4` MEANS
    `the days the table offsets for leaving on` (Date 20 12 2011) EQUALS LIST 3, 4
#ASSERT `leaving on 20.12.2011 is given 3 days and 4`

-- Every other day of the year has exactly one row.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN d YIELD count (`the days the table offsets for leaving on` d) EQUALS 1)
            (LIST Date 1 9 2011, Date 9 10 2011, Date 10 10 2011, Date 19 12 2011, Date 21 12 2011,
                  Date 29 3 2012, Date 30 3 2012, Date 30 6 2012, Date 31 8 2012)

-- The reading adopted (F-2012-13_tashag_01-a): the row that opens on a day
-- governs it, so a teacher leaving on 20.12.2011 is offset 4 days.
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the vacation days offset for leaving on` d IS
    BRANCH IF d AT LEAST (Date 30 3 2012)  THEN 5
           IF d AT LEAST (Date 20 12 2011) THEN 4
           IF d AT LEAST (Date 10 10 2011) THEN 3
           OTHERWISE 0

#ASSERT all (GIVEN d YIELD `the days the table offsets for leaving on` d EQUALS LIST (`the vacation days offset for leaving on` d))
            (LIST Date 1 9 2011, Date 9 10 2011, Date 10 10 2011, Date 19 12 2011, Date 21 12 2011,
                  Date 29 3 2012, Date 30 3 2012, Date 31 8 2012)

-- F-2012-13_tashag_01-b: the section is headed for teachers who left "at
-- the end of 2011/12", but three of its four rows end months before the
-- year does (its salary runs to 26.8.2012), so they can only meet a teacher
-- who left during the year. The reading adopted: the offset applies to every
-- teacher who left or retired from 2011/12, by the date of leaving. The
-- section states what the Ministry does for its own teachers; the owners,
-- to whom the circular is addressed, are read as doing the same.
`three of the four rows end before the year does` MEANS
    count (filter (GIVEN r YIELD r's `left until` LESS THAN (Date 26 8 2012)) `the table of days offset`)
    EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `three of the four rows end before the year does`

GIVEN t IS A `transition teacher`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the vacation offset` t IS
    IF t's `situation` EQUALS `left or retired from 2011/12`
    THEN `the vacation days offset for leaving on` (t's `date of leaving`)
         TIMES t's `day rate in August 2012`
    ELSE 0

@export default The settlement circular תשע"ג/1 makes for one teaching employee across the early opening of 2012/13 — the August salary, plus the September difference or the five extra days, less the offset of the extra vacation days
GIVEN t IS A `transition teacher` @desc the employee
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the transition settlement` t IS
    `the August salary` t
    PLUS `the September difference` t
    PLUS `the five extra days` t
    MINUS `the vacation offset` t

GIVEN t IS A `transition teacher`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `transition action`
DECIDE `offsetting the extra vacation` t IS
    IF t's `situation` EQUALS `left or retired from 2011/12`
    THEN PARTY `the employer`
         MUST  `offset the extra vacation days` `amount`
               PROVIDED `amount` EQUALS `the vacation offset` t
         WITHIN 12
         LEST BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "section 3: the extra vacation days are offset at the August rate"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- akn:conclusions The sign-off and signature; no rule.

-- Worked examples; the rates are round placeholders.
`a continuing teacher whose seniority rose` MEANS
    `transition teacher` WITH
        `situation`                          IS `continuing with the same employer`
        `August salary on the 2011/12 basis` IS 8000
        `day rate in August 2012`            IS 300
        `day rate in September 2012`         IS 320
        `position, grade, seniority or allowances changed` IS TRUE
        `on maternity leave from 27.8.2012`  IS FALSE
        `hired from the August 2012 salary`  IS FALSE
        `date of leaving`                    IS Date 1 9 2012

#ASSERT `the September difference` `a continuing teacher whose seniority rose` EQUALS 100
#ASSERT `the transition settlement` `a continuing teacher whose seniority rose` EQUALS 8100

`a new teacher taken on in September` MEANS
    `transition teacher` WITH
        `situation`                          IS `new with the employer in 2012/13`
        `August salary on the 2011/12 basis` IS 0
        `day rate in August 2012`            IS 0
        `day rate in September 2012`         IS 250
        `position, grade, seniority or allowances changed` IS FALSE
        `on maternity leave from 27.8.2012`  IS FALSE
        `hired from the August 2012 salary`  IS FALSE
        `date of leaving`                    IS Date 1 9 2012

#ASSERT `the five extra days` `a new teacher taken on in September` EQUALS 1250

`a teacher who retired in June` MEANS
    `transition teacher` WITH
        `situation`                          IS `left or retired from 2011/12`
        `August salary on the 2011/12 basis` IS 9000
        `day rate in August 2012`            IS 400
        `day rate in September 2012`         IS 0
        `position, grade, seniority or allowances changed` IS FALSE
        `on maternity leave from 27.8.2012`  IS FALSE
        `hired from the August 2012 salary`  IS FALSE
        `date of leaving`                    IS Date 30 6 2012

#ASSERT `the vacation offset` `a teacher who retired in June` EQUALS 2000
#ASSERT `the transition settlement` `a teacher who retired in June` EQUALS 7000

#TRACE `paying August in full` `a continuing teacher whose seniority rose` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `pay the August salary` 8000 AT 12
#TRACE `settling the difference with September's salary` `a continuing teacher whose seniority rose` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `pay or offset the September difference` 100 AT 13
#TRACE `paying the five extra days` `a new teacher taken on in September` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `pay the five extra days` 1250 AT 14
#TRACE `offsetting the extra vacation` `a teacher who retired in June` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `offset the extra vacation days` 2000 AT 12
